226:| 1 | Give native candidate inspection a private view. Publish only after the pass finishes its required validations. Start with one input and one fresh output ID. | The use of the caller's live IRStore for preparing the candidate. | Reuse the two cases in `scripts/01-pass-boundary.mjs:58`. After rejection both store heads and history of accepted outputs must be unchanged. Add a concurrent stale-head test and a retry. Preserve diagnostic access to the rejected candidate. |
227:| 2 | Introduce explicit acceptance mode, reference semantics, method and quantified scope in results. Wrap Tix exact and tolerance gates first, then the CUDA batch. | The default-to-exact inference and the CUDA scalar stub on the batch-only path. | Unknown method → unknown assurance. Split stays rejected under immediate exact and accepted only on the chosen tolerance cases. Inject a failing executor and distinguish unavailable from refuted. Compare per-function/per-arm coverage, including empty shapes and all-inconclusive runs. `scripts/01-pass-boundary.mjs:17`, `src/tensor/cuda-contract.ts:153`, `src/framework/contracts/differential.ts:291`. |
228:| 3 | Add named projection and coverage requirements to one Tix inline and one lowering. Check endpoint sets and entry coverage separately. | Hand wiring of kernel entity lists and implicit same-ID provenance as the entire explanation for inline. | Test two functions, an unused parameter, removal, empty mapping, and a producer merged into two consumers. Trace a statement through inline and lowering. Check that unrelated functions are outside the declared selection and that the projection boundary composes. `scripts/01-pass-boundary.mjs:27`, `src/tensor/cuda-contract.ts:93`, `src/framework/ir/correspondence.ts:158`. |
229:| 4 | Bind a transformation plus its validation policy as a strategy algorithm. Use one fork of inline/split and choose among accepted arms. Admit an inapplicable arm and an unavailable arm explicitly. | Tix's name-dispatch loop when parity is demonstrated; removes the case for the T6-E/H duplicate operator switches. | For the same inputs compare direct and planned outcomes, revisions, checks, reasons, evidence and origin. Compare synchronous call overhead and end-to-end time. Keep an immediate public entry only where a caller requires it. Preserve different baseline choices for exact and tolerance. `src/tensor/index.ts:32`, `src/framework/passes/bridge.ts:29`, `src/tensor/contract.ts:125`. |
230:| 5 | Make one Typed table rewrite and one Tix substitution emit witnesses. Add declared structural edit for changing entry. Derive local/fact/structural census and D1 ownership bins as queries. | Per-cell table replay for **new** witnessed edits, heuristics for identifying a new entry, and duplicated joins for revision-to-site observations. | Replay the whole candidate. Mutate a sibling operand, stale premise, target revision and rule fingerprint. Record proof coverage per edit, function and whole application separately. Reproduce both A0 policies and D1 conservation; report ambiguous weight rather than duplicating it at multiple parents. `scripts/06-rewrite-scope.mjs:14`, `tests/typed/attribute.test.mjs:43`, **B1-G** `src/typed/specialize-buffer.ts:293`. |
231:| 6 | Register two demands: Tix read/axis summaries per function and B1-G's offline division per function and bindings. Port one dependency propagation to the merged solver. | Repeated planner scans and one BTA iteration loop; leave the domain transfer functions in place. | Compare all cells/locals against the old facts at joins, loops and unreachable blocks. Change the bound buffer or a callee without changing the function text. Count transfer visits, cache hit rate, independent recomputations, wall time and peak bytes. Keep a plain scan if query overhead costs more than repeated work. `src/tensor/fusion.ts:97`, `src/typed/parts.ts:13`, **B1-G** `src/typed/bta.ts:91`, `scripts/02-binding-times.mjs:36`. |
232:| 7 | Extract interning of residual control points from two B1 paths. Keep static operand semantics, alias analysis and guard generation in the domain. | Repeated queues, state-key construction and residual backedge plumbing. | Compare residual programs on the two VM bytecodes with the same inputs, guard and backend profile. Measure instructions, emitted statements/bytes, variants, compilation time and execution of fallback. Force budget exhaustion and ensure no partial publication. Compare joining environments vs splitting by live static data. **B1-B** `src/typed/residualize.ts:61`, **B1-F** `src/typed/pe.ts:224`, **B1-G** `src/typed/specialize-buffer.ts:288`. |
233:| 8 | Hoist one Tix fusion decision into schedule data. Give the emitter and runner the same manifest of kernels, variants and gates. Introduce a restricted checker for strip-mining and ordered fold, then test a dependence-based implementation. | Replanning inside emission, planner-equality checking as a semantic requirement, and gate discovery from source text. | Check symbolic identity of the covered iteration set and empty set of reversed dependence pairs. Include extents 0,1,T−1,T,T+1, simultaneous tails and transposed accesses. Re-run the extent-17 counterexample. Force every runtime arm, compare CPU reference and GPU output, then compare paired timings over held-out shapes with warm-up and repeated samples. Choose wider polyhedral machinery only if it accepts valuable legal candidates the restricted checker refuses at acceptable compile cost. `src/tensor/cuda-runtime.ts:142`, `src/tensor/cuda-contract.ts:187`, `scripts/05-reduction-order.mjs:15`. |
