## Layer-by-layer decision

| Layer | What to keep as it is | Where the boundary should move |
|---|---|---|
| Core | Content-derived identity, immutable artifact snapshots, dependency-aware reuse, and policy checks even on a warm cache. The stricter-policy fixture passed in the CPU suite. `src/framework/ir/store.ts:30`, `src/framework/core/runtime.ts:753`, `tests/framework/pass-policy.test.mjs:64`, `scripts/03-merged-fixtures.sh:4`. | A retained candidate, a cached computation and a currently accepted output are distinct states. Publish the accepted head at one boundary. Attach run observations to an invocation so a second profile or benchmark result can coexist with the same artifact hash. `src/framework/core/runtime.ts:395`, `src/tensor/cuda-contract.ts:168`, `scripts/01-pass-boundary.mjs:58`. |
| IR | Native representations, optional logical projections, typed relation kinds, bounded correspondence composition and scoped edit authority. The separation of operation log and actual diff is valuable for auditing. `src/framework/ir/types.ts:64`, `src/framework/ir/README.md:48`, `src/framework/ir/correspondence.ts:148`, `src/framework/ir/PATTERNS-AND-REWRITES.md:109`. | Name each projection and its universe in references. Allow the native builder to emit a logical edit with witnesses. Requiring a full inverse for every read projection gives a poor price for expression matching. Tix's adapter has no rebuild and stores expressions inside attributes; Typed has a value-handle matcher and editor. `src/tensor/ir.ts:105`, `src/tensor/ir.ts:140`, `src/tensor/passes.ts:82`, `src/typed/tx.ts:120`, `src/typed/rules/compile.ts:24`. |
| Contracts | Typed ports, versioned validators, pre/post conditions, fact-transfer verification and external certificate verification. Preserve deterministic differential generation, delegated deciding and canonical case fingerprint checks. `src/framework/contracts/analysis-manager.ts:885`, `src/framework/contracts/analysis-manager.ts:1226`, `src/framework/contracts/differential.ts:209`, `src/framework/contracts/differential.ts:356`. | Make the reference semantics, domain of inputs, comparator, quantifier and validator explicit. Permit batch-only evaluation. CUDA currently supplies a throwing subject runner because the scalar runner is mandatory, and separately maps infrastructure failure into accepted=false. `src/framework/contracts/differential.ts:49`, `src/tensor/cuda-contract.ts:153`, `src/tensor/cuda-contract.ts:169`, `src/tensor/cuda-contract.ts:253`. |
| Passes | Write-set checking, native or projected candidate construction and recomputation as a fallback for a preservation claim. Preserve the no-edit fast path. `src/framework/passes/define-pass.ts:216`, `src/framework/passes/define-pass.ts:302`, `src/framework/passes/define-pass.ts:315`, `src/framework/passes/define-pass.ts:373`. | Make an optimization a same-port instance of transformation. Give both execution modes the same specification and outcomes; determine at plan construction which capabilities a synchronous host can supply. Give identity proposals a `no-change` outcome so reports distinguish them from a new equivalence check. `src/framework/passes/define-pass.ts:225`, `src/framework/passes/define-pass.ts:250`, `src/tensor/index.ts:44`. |
| Dataflow | Lattice/transfer separation, worklist and sweep schedules, edge refinement, explicit widening and bounded nonconvergence. Typed liveness, reaching definitions and ranges supply distinct instances. `src/framework/dataflow/solver.ts:24`, `src/framework/dataflow/solver.ts:90`, `src/typed/analyses.ts:296`, `src/typed/analyses.ts:352`, `src/typed/analyses.ts:486`. | Keep the solver available to analyses over finite dependence graphs. Let a registered analysis also call a symbolic relation algorithm or a direct traversal. Tix's affine read relation and ordered reductions are a poor match for CFG joins; the production planner currently computes them directly. `src/tensor/fusion.ts:83`, `src/tensor/ir.ts:123`, `src/framework/dataflow/analysis.ts:153`, `scripts/02-binding-times.mjs:36`. |
| Strategy | Versioned declarative plans, recoverable alternatives, independent branches, budgets, metrics and recorded selection. Typed chooses pipelines with these operations; the merged strategy fixture exercises all 13 node kinds. `src/typed/strategies.ts:175`, `src/framework/strategy/interpreter.ts:443`, `tests/framework/strategy.test.mjs:27`, `scripts/03-merged-fixtures.sh:4`. | Keep one strategy semantics. Domain-defined kernels may run immediately, dispatch to workers, or await device observations. Keep compile-time selection distinct from a generated runtime shape guard. Tix currently does the latter and parses arm IDs out of emitted source. `src/tensor/fusion.ts:136`, `src/tensor/cuda-runtime.ts:142`, **T6-J** `src/tensor/schedule-plan.ts:45`. |

The import evidence is specific to the merged tensor implementation. Its two optimization registrations build native modules, its optimizer directly maps a list of names, and its lowering directly calls the planner. Searching the tensor sources found no framework dataflow or rewrite-engine use. The matcher hit in the parser is JavaScript string matching. The framework's generic rewrite engine has valuable scheduling and match evidence; there is no reason to route a whole-function fusion planner through it merely to increase adoption. `src/tensor/passes.ts:82`, `src/tensor/index.ts:35`, `src/tensor/index.ts:66`, `src/tensor/parser.ts:32`, `src/framework/ir/PATTERNS-AND-REWRITES.md:74`.

## Proposed concepts and their smallest instances

The evidence supports extracting the following *interfaces*. The signatures, division of ownership and proposed evaluation criteria are design hypotheses. “Domain” below means the implementer supplies the operators' semantics, layout, aliasing, floating-point model and measurement method. A generic validator cannot infer those by inspecting JSON.

### 1. Partial transformation with a single publication boundary
**Promote empirical thresholds into universal cost facts.** I would decline. Keep the shape predicate, selected arm and observation protocol as reproducible data. A prediction may propose a choice. A measured choice is evidence on the measured shapes and hardware profile. Tie the winner to that comparison and retain the fallback arm and uncertainty. This also applies to Typed speed versus O2. Add a new cost-analysis package only after both clients agree on an observation protocol and on which quantities are comparable. `src/tensor/fusion.ts:107`, `src/tensor/fusion.ts:135`, `src/typed/strategies.ts:66`, `src/typed/strategies.ts:175`, `BACKLOG.md:485`.

## Migration with decision points

Each step can land without a new production implementation of the later steps. The deletions below are targets after parity. All measurements are proposed unless identified as probe results.

| Order | Small change and first client | What it deletes | Check and decision |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | Give native candidate inspection a private view. Publish only after the pass finishes its required validations. Start with one input and one fresh output ID. | The use of the caller's live IRStore for preparing the candidate. | Reuse the two cases in `scripts/01-pass-boundary.mjs:58`. After rejection both store heads and history of accepted outputs must be unchanged. Add a concurrent stale-head test and a retry. Preserve diagnostic access to the rejected candidate. |
| 2 | Introduce explicit acceptance mode, reference semantics, method and quantified scope in results. Wrap Tix exact and tolerance gates first, then the CUDA batch. | The default-to-exact inference and the CUDA scalar stub on the batch-only path. | Unknown method → unknown assurance. Split stays rejected under immediate exact and accepted only on the chosen tolerance cases. Inject a failing executor and distinguish unavailable from refuted. Compare per-function/per-arm coverage, including empty shapes and all-inconclusive runs. `scripts/01-pass-boundary.mjs:17`, `src/tensor/cuda-contract.ts:153`, `src/framework/contracts/differential.ts:291`. |
| 3 | Add named projection and coverage requirements to one Tix inline and one lowering. Check endpoint sets and entry coverage separately. | Hand wiring of kernel entity lists and implicit same-ID provenance as the entire explanation for inline. | Test two functions, an unused parameter, removal, empty mapping, and a producer merged into two consumers. Trace a statement through inline and lowering. Check that unrelated functions are outside the declared selection and that the projection boundary composes. `scripts/01-pass-boundary.mjs:27`, `src/tensor/cuda-contract.ts:93`, `src/framework/ir/correspondence.ts:158`. |
| 4 | Bind a transformation plus its validation policy as a strategy algorithm. Use one fork of inline/split and choose among accepted arms. Admit an inapplicable arm and an unavailable arm explicitly. | Tix's name-dispatch loop when parity is demonstrated; removes the case for the T6-E/H duplicate operator switches. | For the same inputs compare direct and planned outcomes, revisions, checks, reasons, evidence and origin. Compare synchronous call overhead and end-to-end time. Keep an immediate public entry only where a caller requires it. Preserve different baseline choices for exact and tolerance. `src/tensor/index.ts:32`, `src/framework/passes/bridge.ts:29`, `src/tensor/contract.ts:125`. |
| 5 | Make one Typed table rewrite and one Tix substitution emit witnesses. Add declared structural edit for changing entry. Derive local/fact/structural census and D1 ownership bins as queries. | Per-cell table replay for **new** witnessed edits, heuristics for identifying a new entry, and duplicated joins for revision-to-site observations. | Replay the whole candidate. Mutate a sibling operand, stale premise, target revision and rule fingerprint. Record proof coverage per edit, function and whole application separately. Reproduce both A0 policies and D1 conservation; report ambiguous weight rather than duplicating it at multiple parents. `scripts/06-rewrite-scope.mjs:14`, `tests/typed/attribute.test.mjs:43`, **B1-G** `src/typed/specialize-buffer.ts:293`. |
| 6 | Register two demands: Tix read/axis summaries per function and B1-G's offline division per function and bindings. Port one dependency propagation to the merged solver. | Repeated planner scans and one BTA iteration loop; leave the domain transfer functions in place. | Compare all cells/locals against the old facts at joins, loops and unreachable blocks. Change the bound buffer or a callee without changing the function text. Count transfer visits, cache hit rate, independent recomputations, wall time and peak bytes. Keep a plain scan if query overhead costs more than repeated work. `src/tensor/fusion.ts:97`, `src/typed/parts.ts:13`, **B1-G** `src/typed/bta.ts:91`, `scripts/02-binding-times.mjs:36`. |
| 7 | Extract interning of residual control points from two B1 paths. Keep static operand semantics, alias analysis and guard generation in the domain. | Repeated queues, state-key construction and residual backedge plumbing. | Compare residual programs on the two VM bytecodes with the same inputs, guard and backend profile. Measure instructions, emitted statements/bytes, variants, compilation time and execution of fallback. Force budget exhaustion and ensure no partial publication. Compare joining environments vs splitting by live static data. **B1-B** `src/typed/residualize.ts:61`, **B1-F** `src/typed/pe.ts:224`, **B1-G** `src/typed/specialize-buffer.ts:288`. |
| 8 | Hoist one Tix fusion decision into schedule data. Give the emitter and runner the same manifest of kernels, variants and gates. Introduce a restricted checker for strip-mining and ordered fold, then test a dependence-based implementation. | Replanning inside emission, planner-equality checking as a semantic requirement, and gate discovery from source text. | Check symbolic identity of the covered iteration set and empty set of reversed dependence pairs. Include extents 0,1,T−1,T,T+1, simultaneous tails and transposed accesses. Re-run the extent-17 counterexample. Force every runtime arm, compare CPU reference and GPU output, then compare paired timings over held-out shapes with warm-up and repeated samples. Choose wider polyhedral machinery only if it accepts valuable legal candidates the restricted checker refuses at acceptable compile cost. `src/tensor/cuda-runtime.ts:142`, `src/tensor/cuda-contract.ts:187`, `scripts/05-reduction-order.mjs:15`. |

**Stop condition for framework growth.** If the second instance needs unrelated revisions of an abstraction, retain two domain implementations and share only the smaller demonstrated law. If a new check rejects a formerly accepted input, classify the case as a real counterexample, a stricter policy, unsupported semantics or a checker defect before comparing speed. Report compiler and validator cost separately. A stronger checker and a faster kernel answer independent research questions.

## Open questions

1. **What counts as published to a client?** A caller may want rejected candidates to remain inspectable. Can a separate candidate store serve that purpose while accepted heads, fact transfer and strategy selection share one commit decision? The fresh-output-ID case is a concrete acceptance test. `scripts/01-pass-boundary.mjs:64`.
2. **How small can a witness be?** Start with a verified rule, focus path and fact IDs. Compare trace size, replay cost and fraction of full revisions covered against a structural diff. A0 recovers a substantial numerator, but the denominator changes markedly with scope. **A0-G** `ttmp/2026/11/27/IRWB-035-G--what-share-of-the-optimizer-s-edits-are-local-value-rewrites/reference/02-report-the-share-of-local-value-rewrites-among-the-optimizer-s-edits.md:66`.

