     1	/**
     2	 * Loop rotation by header duplication (IRWB-003, agenda item G1). A loop's header that is only its test,
     3	 * `if c goto T else E`, is copied into every block that jumps to it unconditionally: the preheader's copy is the
     4	 * guard (does the loop run at all), the latch's copy is the bottom test (does it run again). The header then has
     5	 * no predecessor and is pruned. An iteration ends with one conditional branch instead of a jump and a branch,
     6	 * once the backend's layout ('loops') puts the latch's exit after it.
     7	 *
     8	 * Valid whatever the test reads or does: it is tail duplication. Each path that jumped to the header runs a copy
     9	 * of it at the point where it would have run the original, once. When both T and E are inside the loop (the
    10	 * first half of an `&&`), the rotated loop has two entries and is irreducible; analyses still terminate (the
    11	 * solver widens at every retreating edge), and passes that need natural loops (licm) no longer see it, so
    12	 * rotation runs after them. The condition may not call or read a result leaf, which keeps leaves next to their
    13	 * calls.
    14	 *
    15	 * The spec is wrapped by `typedPass` in passes.ts (`rotate`), which registers it; this module imports only types
    16	 * from there, so the two do not form a cycle at load time.
    17	 */
